Mia Wang: Quick check: if someone lands from an external link into a compact left nav, should the top breadcrumb row remain visible or should the workspace name live only in the page header? Noticed filters drop when we use short links :thinking_face:
Omar Khan: Context first. I prefer a tiny, single-line breadcrumb so users know "where" they are. If we remove it we must surface workspace + route in an always-visible header band.
Jamie Lee: We have two URL shapes in the wild: `/workspace/123/models/xyz` and `/models/xyz?ws=123`. Marketing uses the query form because it's shorter. We need a deterministic canonical route to avoid hydration surprises.
Mia Wang: Agreed. UX preference: condensed breadcrumb in compact mode (14px, single line) that truncates long workspace names with ellipsis and exposes full text on long-press/tap for mobile.
Nora Patel: Accessibility note: condensed crumbs must still be keyboard focusable, each crumb needs `aria-current` on the active one, and truncated text needs `aria-label` containing the full name. For mobile long-press, ensure the context sheet is reachable by screen readers and sets `role=dialog`.
Omar Khan: Routing contract idea: canonical = `/w/:ws/...` (path-based), fallback = query param form. On app boot, we should rewrite fallback form to canonical for internal routing (client-side replace) so tracking and logs are consistent. Also add `?preserveNav=0|1` for embeds.
Jamie Lee: For legacy links using hash fragments like `#panel=metrics`, we should migrate them to `?panel=metrics` during initial route parse and capture telemetry so we can estimate how many bookmarks are old.
Mia Wang: How about a small visual compromise: show condensed breadcrumb but hide workspace if compact width < 320px; on mobile tap it opens an action sheet with "copy link", "open parent", and the full path.
lexi-design-bot: New draft spec: https://redwood.design/ux/landing-context-preserve — includes condensed breadcrumb visuals and mobile sheet patterns. Canary deploy scheduled after UX sign-off.
a11y-bot: A11y checklist added to spec: 1) nav landmark around crumbs, 2) `aria-current="page"` for active crumb, 3) truncated crumbs include `aria-label`, 4) focus outline meets 4.5:1 contrast, 5) mobile sheet announced via `aria-modal` and initial focus.
Jamie Lee: We'll put a small router migration in the frontend RFC. Pseudocode for hydration (note: different from earlier proposal):
```
// run on first render
function migrateLegacyUrl() {
  const url = new URL(window.location.href);
  // move `ws` query -> path if query-form used
  if (url.searchParams.has('ws') && url.pathname.startsWith('/models/')) {
    const ws = url.searchParams.get('ws');
    const modelId = url.pathname.split('/').pop();
    const canonical = `/w/${ws}/models/${modelId}`;
    window.history.replaceState({}, '', canonical + url.search);
    telemetry.trackEvent('migrate_query_ws_to_path');
  }
  // hash -> query migration
  if (window.location.hash.includes('panel=')) {
    const hashParams = new URLSearchParams(window.location.hash.substring(1));
    const panel = hashParams.get('panel');
    if (panel) {
      url.searchParams.set('panel', panel);
      window.history.replaceState({}, '', url.pathname + '?' + url.searchParams.toString());
      telemetry.trackEvent('migrate_hash_panel');
    }
  }
}
```
Omar Khan: We'll also add a `preserveNav` flag defaulting to 1 for web; embeds (iframes) will set `preserveNav=0` to hide crumbs. Router should never encode UI-only state into path segments; use query params for ephemeral panel state.
Nora Patel: Microcopy nit: in the mobile sheet action, use "Open parent workspace" instead of "Open workspace" for clarity. Also provide a visible label for the breadcrumb toggle that reads "Show path" for screen readers.
Mia Wang: I'll update Sketch and include condensed breadcrumb examples at 320/360/412 widths. I'll also add hover and long-press specs and a small animation for the sheet so it's clear it's contextual.
Jamie Lee: Sounds good. I'll add the RFC entry and ask infra to whitelist the client-side redirects so they don't get blocked by CSP.
Omar Khan: One more ops note: emit `legacy_url_mapped` event whenever we rewrite an incoming URL so we can create a dashboard for these events and monitor for regressions.
Mia Wang: Thanks! I'll post the updated frames here when ready and tag @Nora for accessibility review. :sparkles:
